   "widgets_values": [
    "hand-drawn pictorial map symbol in the manner of an illustrated storybook atlas, monochrome sepia: one warm brown hue and nothing else, no other colour anywhere, bold dark sepia ink contour of uneven hand-pressed weight drawn freehand with a slightly wobbling line, the outline almost black-brown and far darker than anything it encloses, strong contrast between that dark outline and the pale tan tone filling the shapes, shaded only by fine parallel hatching and short cross-hatching in the same dark ink on the side away from the light, gently stylised and charming rather than technical, simplified massing with steep exaggerated roofs, tall slender towers and oversized doorways, drawn in flat side elevation as a symbol cut out and floating free with nothing whatsoever underneath it, not as a scale drawing, no perspective recession, even flat lighting with the shade thrown consistently to the lower right, historically accurate 12th to 14th century European material culture, heavy readable line weight that still reads at thumbnail size, matte, a fairy-tale castle drawn as a map symbol, a cluster of slender towers with tall conical spires and pennants rising above a walled keep, storybook proportions, single map symbol drawn in flat side elevation, pure white background, no parchment, nothing at all beneath the object, no ground line, no ground plate, no cast shadow, centred with generous margin, 1:1 square"
   ],
   "title": "Prompt = STYLE_CORE + subject + canvas"
